### IPP-1715 Coding problems API
### First, in the server folder:
###   npm run import:problems -- javascript          (dry run: "5 problems checked", added 5)
###   npm run import:problems -- javascript --yes    (saves)
### Put ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Guest list -> 200, hasAccess false, topics [{ name "Strings", total 5, free 5 }], 5 problems, isLocked false
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems?language=javascript


### 2. Guest, free problem -> 200, hints has 1 item, hintsTotal 3, solution null, solutionLocked true,
###    tests 8, nav { index 4, total 5, prev "count-vowels", next "valid-anagram" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems/javascript/capitalize-every-word


### 3. Admin login -> 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 4. Admin, same problem -> 200, hasAccess true, hints 3, solution.code and solution.explanation present
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems/javascript/capitalize-every-word
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 5. Unknown problem -> 404 "Problem not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems/javascript/no-such-problem


### 6. Unknown language -> 404 "Language not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems?language=python


### 7. Missing language -> 400 "Invalid language"
GET {{baseUrl}}/problems


### 8. Locked problem (only after a Pro topic is added, e.g. Arrays) -> guest gets 403, code NEEDS_FULL_ACCESS
# GET {{baseUrl}}/problems/javascript/<a-pro-problem-slug>
